`ctlv.h` is a header whose only content is `struct ctlv_cursor` plus forward declarations. Of the forward declarations, `ctlv_device`, `ctlv_family`, `ctlv_op_ctx` and `ctlv_schema_tree` are not used in this header at all except `ctlv_schema_tree` (in the cursor); `ctlv_device`/`ctlv_family`/`ctlv_op_ctx` are dead here. Only `ctlv_msg` and `ctlv_schema_tree` are needed. The file comment says "CTLV family API" but it contains no API, and there is also no declaration of the entry points families use (`ctlv_input_*`/`ctlv_output_*`, registration); those are presumably in `drivers/ctlv/*.h` or elsewhere, so "Add the in-kernel API used by family implementations" in the commit message overstates what is here.

