Derive the limits instead of halving: reserve what the driver core adds around this callback (`ACTION`, `DEVPATH`, `SUBSYSTEM`, `MAJOR`, `MINOR`, `DEVNAME`, `DEVMODE`, `DEVUID`, `DEVGID`, `DEVTYPE`, `SEQNUM`, `HOME`, `PATH`) and give CTLV the rest. List those names in an enum ending in a count (`CTLV_UEVENT_CORE_VARS`), so the number cannot drift from the list, and define `CTLV_UEVENT_MAX_VARS` as `UEVENT_NUM_ENVP - CTLV_UEVENT_CORE_VARS`. The byte reserve cannot be counted (`DEVPATH` dominates), so it stays an estimate with a comment.

